schema: "0.4"
id: scholar-09-graded-projects
type: image
quality: high

# The Robot Learns — a terminal study CLI. Graded Projects — a grader sub-agent's rubric
# evaluation of a submitted hands-on project, in a clean LIGHT terminal.
# Theme tenets: light-native near-white canvas, single indigo accent, crisp 4px radius, thin
# visible gray borders (structure from lines), Inter labels + JetBrains Mono for scores/ids.
# Palette: canvas #fafafa, ink #111118, alt #f5f5f5, border #e0e0e0, indigo #6366F1;
# semantic success #22c55e, warning #eab308 (used only as small per-criterion markers).

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a clean LIGHT
    terminal window showing a graded-project evaluation — a rubric feedback report from a
    grader sub-agent. Precise, calm, exacting; grading clarity is the point, so every
    criterion, score and citation must be legible and the assessment must feel fair and
    structured. Near-white terminal canvas (a light-mode terminal), NOT dark. Clean humanist
    sans (Inter) for criteria and feedback prose; a matched monospace for the grade figure,
    per-criterion scores and citation paths. One single indigo accent; semantic green/amber
    appear only as small markers beside labels.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity mockup of a clean LIGHT terminal window — "The Robot Learns" —
    showing the graded result of a hands-on project. One near-white terminal pane fills the
    frame. This is a light-mode terminal (near-white canvas, dark ink), NOT a dark terminal
    and NOT a browser page.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (a title bar, a grade header, a rubric list, a citations footer):
    - TITLE BAR: minimal terminal chrome — three small dots and a mono title
      "the-robot-learns — /project grade", closed by a thin hairline.
    - GRADE HEADER: a score / results summary line — the project title in sans beside an
      overall grade as a mono figure "Score 88 / 100 · Pass" with a small indigo-outlined
      status chip; a thin indigo summary bar beneath.
    - PROJECT RUBRIC FEEDBACK BLOCK (dominant): a vertical list of rubric criteria, each a
      bordered row — the criterion name in sans, a small per-criterion mono score "18/20",
      and one or two lines of grader feedback in muted prose; a 2px indigo left rail marks
      the criterion currently expanded. Passed criteria carry a small green check; the one
      weak criterion carries a muted amber marker — color used sparingly beside a label,
      never on its own.
    - CITATION LIST (footer): a "References" group — a few mono citation rows linking KB
      articles, e.g. "kb://networking/ingress-tls · Rate limiting", in indigo link color,
      quiet.

    A faint mono status line: "graded by rubric · cited 3 KB articles · :open a citation".

    PALETTE & TYPE: near-white terminal canvas; deep near-black ink for criterion names and
    the grade figure; muted gray for feedback prose; a single saturated indigo for the
    summary bar, the active left rail, and the citation links; semantic success-green and
    warning-amber only as small per-criterion markers beside text. Criterion names and
    feedback in a clean humanist sans; the grade figure, per-criterion scores and citation
    paths in a matched monospace.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: crisp small 4px rounded corners on the rubric rows and status chip;
    thin visible cool-gray borders separate each criterion row (structure from lines, not
    shadow); flat surfaces, no elevation beyond a single faint shadow if any. No gradients,
    no glow, no texture.

    MOOD: precise, trustworthy, exacting — grading clarity, where every criterion and
    citation is legible and the assessment reads as fair and structured.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, browser chrome, address bar, browser tabs, web page, dark terminal, dark mode, black background, neon glow, gradient background, rainbow of accent colors"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches Graded Projects: an overall grade/score summary header, a per-criterion rubric feedback list with scores and feedback prose, and a citation list linking KB articles — inside a terminal pane"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Light-native near-white terminal canvas, a single indigo accent with green/amber only as small per-criterion markers, crisp 4px radius, thin visible gray borders, Inter prose + monospace for scores/ids — not a dark terminal, not generic UI"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Clear header-to-rubric-to-citations hierarchy; a scannable criteria list; plausible real-product terminal layout"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "dark terminal / dark mode instead of a light near-white terminal"
    - "browser chrome, tabs, or address bar instead of a terminal window"
    - "semantic colors used as large fills rather than small markers beside labels"

tags: [scholar, therobotlearns.com, screen-mockup, terminal]
